## `installer/README.md`

```markdown
# CygnusAgentSetup.exe

FIX: this used to be spec-only (no actual installer source in the repo).
The WiX v4 source now lives at `CygnusAgentSetup.wxs` in this folder and
implements every step below — see that file's inline comments for the
1:1 mapping.

## Build

```
dotnet publish ..\src\CygnusAgent.Service -c Release -r win-x64 ^
  -p:PublishProfile=win-x64-selfcontained -o .\payload

wix build CygnusAgentSetup.wxs -d PayloadDir=.\payload -o CygnusAgentSetup.msi
```

Requires the WiX v4 CLI (`dotnet tool install --global wix`) on the BUILD
machine only — never on the end-user's machine.

## Command line (end user / RMM)

```
CygnusAgentSetup.exe /enroll:<token>          interactive install
CygnusAgentSetup.exe /quiet /enroll:<token>   silent install for GPO/RMM
```

## What it does, in order (implemented in CygnusAgentSetup.wxs)

1. Copies the published, self-contained `CygnusAgent.Service.exe` to
   `%ProgramFiles%\CygnusAgent\` — no separate .NET runtime install needed
   on the target machine (see `CygnusAgent.Service.csproj`'s
   self-contained/single-file publish settings).
2. Registers the Windows Event Log source `CygnusAgent`
   (`util:EventSource` element).
3. Creates `%ProgramData%\CygnusAgent\` and locks its ACLs to SYSTEM +
   Administrators (`util:PermissionEx` elements on `DataDirAcl`).
4. Registers the `CygnusAgent` Windows Service, auto-start
   (`ServiceInstall`/`ServiceControl` elements).
5. Passes `/enroll:<token>` as the `CYGNUSENROLLTOKEN` MSI property, set
   as the `CYGNUS_ENROLL_TOKEN` environment variable — read once by
   `AgentWorker.EnsureEnrolledAsync` and never persisted to disk.
6. Starts the service (`ServiceControl Start="install"`).
7. `/quiet` suppresses UI via `WixUI_Minimal`; MSI's own exit codes are
   non-zero on failure, so RMM tooling can detect a failed install without
   a custom action.

## What it must never do

- Never embed a permanent API key or credential in the install command.
- Never write the enrollment token to disk.
- Never install with a debug/dev-mode bypass compiled in.

## Uninstall

Standard MSI uninstall (`msiexec /x`): stops and removes the service
(`ServiceControl Remove="uninstall"`) and offers to delete
`%ProgramData%\CygnusAgent\`.

```

